        "id": "intro",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Three Ways to Fix a Flat Image\n\nDraws a dull, low-contrast title card and fixes it three ways, side by side. Every step runs in the editor process, with no file, model or key.\n\n**How it works:** \"1 Gradient\", \"2 Title\" and \"3 Grain\" draw the flat image, and \"4 Flat image\" adds the grain. \"Auto contrast\" stretches the levels so 1% of the pixels clip at each end. \"Equalize\" flattens the histogram. \"Adaptive\" equalizes each tile of an 8 by 8 grid, with a clip limit against noise.\n\n**Try this:** Set Clip Limit on \"Adaptive\" to 4 for a stronger local effect, or connect your own image to \"4 Flat image\"."
        },
